summary: Test for CPU soft hotplugging
description: |
    Author: William Gomeringer <wgomerin@redhat.com>

    Description:

    This test tries to test CPU soft hotplug - logically online/offline hotplug.

    a) Basic: Tries offline and online each CPU core.

    b) Continous: This test tries to logically offline or online random CPU
                  core for ~10 min (see CONTIME variable). It's about 600-900
                  hotplug events (CPU ups/downs).

    PASS on no kernel panic or kernel oops or no cpu core stuck.

    The test is usually able to do ~60-90 hotplug events within 1 minute.
contact: William Gomeringer <wgomerin@redhat.com>
component:
  - kernel
test: ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
recommend:
  - kernel
duration: 1h
id: 105e04e5-730f-4218-b8cb-60546ef894fe
extra-summary: /kernel/hotplug/cpusofthotplug
extra-task: /kernel/hotplug/cpusofthotplug
